  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 141 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nFor Friday onward, high pressure starts to reinforce itself across\nthe region. This will start the return of hot and dry conditions\nagain. High temperatures near 104 degrees are forecast across the\nBig Country on Saturday. Similar conditions will continue into the\nearly part of next week, but with slightly cooler temperatures.\nLong range models continue to show a weakened high pressure ridge\nby the middle to end of next week. This may allow for cooler\ntemperatures and a few low chances (20%) for rain. This remains\nrather uncertain at this point, however.",
